<title>HONG KONG: Hongkong Telecom shrs up after VOD deal.</title>
<headline>Hongkong Telecom shrs up after VOD deal.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong Telecommunications Ltd shares edged up after it secured a local film supply for its interactive television services and announced plans to launch its video-on-demand (VOD) services in July, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Anticipation of a stronger income base from its launch of interactive television services fueled buying interest,&quot; said a sales manager at a local brokerage.</p>
<p>Hongkong Telecom shares rose HK$0.40 or 2.86 percent to HK$14.40 in late trade on volume of 16.70 million shares.</p>
</text>
